## Managing flares

- agree a **flare plan** with your rheumatology team
- rest the affected joints, but keep gently moving them
- use hot or cold packs
- contact your team's **helpline** if a flare does not settle

## Fatigue

Tiredness is one of the hardest parts of RA. Pace yourself, plan rest, and tell your team, as it can be a sign your RA is not well controlled.

## Exercise

Regular, gentle exercise such as walking, swimming and cycling helps keep joints moving and muscles strong. A physiotherapist can suggest exercises.

## Look after your heart

RA raises the risk of heart disease. **Stopping smoking** is especially important, as smoking also makes RA worse and treatments work less well.

## Emotional support

Living with a long-term condition can affect your mood. Talk to your GP or team if you feel low.

## Support

The **National Rheumatoid Arthritis Society (NRAS)** and **Versus Arthritis** both run free helplines.
